/** Standalone batch AK -- new 4-case standard (Sample + boundary + tricky + stress).
 * All solvers below were independently written and verified byte-for-byte against each problem's
 * real official Sample before being trusted to generate boundary/tricky/stress expected output.
 *
 * uva-12041-bfs-binary-fibonacci-string: character-at-position via recursion on the Fibonacci-like
 *   string definition (BFS(n)=BFS(n-2)+BFS(n-1)), using a precomputed BigInt length table up to
 *   index 100 (Fibonacci growth means length(98) already vastly exceeds the 2^31-1 max index) --
 *   for N beyond that table, the recursion is guaranteed to always take the "left" (n-2) branch, so
 *   N can be reduced directly via parity-matching arithmetic down into the table's range without
 *   iterating billions of times. Verified against all 20 datasets in the real sample.
 * uva-12096-the-setstack-computer: represent each hereditarily-finite set canonically as a sorted,
 *   deduplicated array of child set IDs, interned via a global hash map (so structurally-equal sets
 *   always collapse to the same ID, making union/intersect/equality operations correct and cheap).
 *   Verified against all 5 datasets in the real sample.
 * uva-12195-jingle-composing: note-duration letters (W/H/Q/E/S/T/X) were not scraped as an explicit
 *   table in the statement -- reverse-engineered the standard whole/half/quarter/eighth/sixteenth/
 *   thirty-second/sixty-fourth mapping (64/32/16/8/4/2/1 in 64ths) by hand-verifying it reproduces
 *   the statement's own worked example ("XXXTXTEQH" summing to exactly 64). Verified against all 15
 *   datasets in the real sample.
 * uva-12208-how-many-ones-needed: standard per-bit-position combinatorial count of set bits across
 *   0..N (count(N) - count(a-1) per query), using the closed-form block formula per bit rather than
 *   any iteration over the (up to 2*10^9) range. Verified against all 18 datasets in the real sample.
 * uva-12218-an-industrial-spy: for each non-empty subset of the given digit multiset, generate all
 *   distinct permutations (deduplicating identical-digit swaps via the standard sorted-subset +
 *   used[] technique), parse each as an integer (naturally stripping leading zeros), and count how
 *   many distinct resulting values are prime. Verified against all 26 datasets in the real sample,
 *   including the leading-zero-collapse case ("011" -> 2 primes: 11 and 101).
 * uva-12223-moving-to-nuremberg: classic weighted-tree "minimize sum of round-trip distances to
 *   weighted target vertices" problem, solved via rerooting DP: compute the cost at an arbitrary
 *   root via one BFS, then reroot in a second BFS pass using cost(child) = cost(parent) + edgeWeight
 *   * (totalFreq - 2*subtreeFreq(child)). Verified against all 12 datasets in the real sample.
 * uva-12250-language-detection: direct fixed lookup table for the 6 known greeting words, else
 *   "UNKNOWN". Verified against the real sample's full 24-case listing.
 */
